            "review_title": "Review at Baguette & Chocolat",
            "review_text": "cherrell p\n49 contributions\n1\nDefinitely visit when at museum, social enterprise\nAug 2019\nI didn't eat at this restaurant but really enjoyed a fresh cold coconut juice on a hot day. There was a beautiful breeze as we sat on the veranda surrounded by big trees. It was a very pleasant setting, probably the nicest setting I have found at a restaurant during my 3 months in Hanoi. The thing I really like about this restaurant is that it is part of a training school for disadvantaged young people. The youth that train here are part of some of the most marginalised in Vietnam coming from families who experience hardship most of us could never imagine. If you visit with your children, share the story of the restaurant and the work they do to help young people with little education who come from very poor families, often with parents who have died young and who really have no future except poverty and how this business is giving them hope.\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten August 18, 2019",
            "rating": 5.0,
            "review_date": "2026-10-15",
            "travel_date": "Recent",
            "feature_depth_status": "Schema-Full-Features-Validated"
        },
