            "review_title": "Review at Baguette & Chocolat",
            "review_text": "Mark M\nEl Dorado Hills, California743 contributions\n0\nSurprisingly good for a museum restaurant\nApr 2016 • Couples\nIt's the Wandering Yank here. In my travels I've been to a number of museum cafes and restaurants, usually out of desperation. This was no different - it had been a long day of sightseeing and we were ready by early afternoon for some refreshment and comfortable chairs And we were very pleasantly surprised!\n\nService was excellent and very attentive. The menu is extensive. Mrs. Yank and I shared delicious noodles with chicken, spring rolls and a salad. All were exceedingly fresh and flavorful. We saw ice cream pass by but we resisted. It did look good though - 3 scoops of mixed flavors.\n\nBoth indoor and shaded outdoor seating is available. We opted for the patio under a fan, which was perfect on an 85-degree day.\n\nThe menu said this restaurant's mission is to train disadvantaged youth in the hospitality industry, which made it just that much more interesting and meaningful to us.\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten April 11, 2016",
