            "review_text": "breweruk\nBrookmans Park, United Kingdom3052 contributions\n0\nWonderful experience - delicious food\nApr 2016 • Solo\nThis little cafe in the grounds of the ethnic museum is just amazing. It's run by the Hoa Sua School for disadvantaged youth, who learn how to cook, serve and manage restaurants. And they are great at all they do. This has to be one of the best meals I have had in Vietnam. I sat outside under the shade of trees close to reconstructed ethnic village houses. Music was playing from ethnic groups gathered around a small lake. My spring rolls with noodles were by far the best I have eaten. The morning glory with mushrooms was amazing. And the prices are really good. If you eat here you help the cause, but it's a cause worth supporting because organising and delivering the training are doing an excellent job. Congratulations to them. What a happy experience.\nRead more\nWritten April 10, 2016",
