            "review_text": "Coastliners_HK\n227 contributions\n0\nOk apart for the 'nose' incident.\nOct 2015 • Family\nWe had a very relaxing a lengthy luncheon here as a nice break in our most enjoyable tour of the museum and exhibits.\n\nThe food is pretty average and a little expensive but given it serves a 'captive audience' this was not a surprise.\n\nThe facility serves to train young entrants to the world of hospitality and seems to do a reasonable job in that regard. Our one observation that fell short of expectations given it is a training facility related to hygiene. We saw the young chap on reception walk from his post 'empty his nose' and then wipe his nose with his had which in turn was wiped on his trouser bottom. Having walked back to his post he picked up a menu to offer to an approaching guest.\n\nWe appreciate that we are in SE Asia but at this price point and for a training facility this was a little disappointing.\n\nThat one issue aside it ok. And if the chap hadn't had a cold we would not have had any negative to note.\n\nGive it a try.\nRead more\nWritten November 6, 2015",
